WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:07.879
So there's now a discussion happening about
how soon Joe Biden and Democrats should wait

00:00:07.879 --> 00:00:13.059
for Republicans to negotiate on the covid
relief bill before just going forward and

00:00:13.059 --> 00:00:17.610
passing it without Republican support via
budget reconciliation if Democrats have the

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.660
votes in the Senate.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.410
Now, there are people criticizing Joe Biden.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.070
Why is Joe Biden meeting with Republicans
about the covid bill?

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:28.830
Why is Joe Biden inviting 10 Democrats, 10
Republican senators to meet as he did last

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:29.830
night?

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:32.840
When these people are clearly bad faith actors,
there's not going to be unity.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.330
There's not going to be negotiation.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:38.190
That gets us anything close to what Joe Biden
wants, which is a one point nine trillion

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:39.649
dollar package.

00:00:39.649 --> 00:00:44.220
And I basically agree with all of that other
than to say the meeting is fine.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.960
Let's just understand that after the meeting,
Republicans, as we've already seen them do

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:55.280
this morning, are going to insist that they
want some pathetic 600 billion dollar stimulus

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:00.659
bill, these same senators who now are going
back to the tired old tropes of Republicans,

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:05.010
we can't afford it, but where's the money
going to come from?

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.390
But inflation.

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:08.730
But the debt, but the deficit.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:13.630
People who said nothing as Trump exploded
the deficit despite claiming he would pay

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:20.400
off the entire national debt during his first
term, these same Republican senators gleefully,

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.580
happily voted for 740 billion dollars for
the military budget just recently.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.750
So they are hypocrites.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:31.490
They are exactly who we believed them to be.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:36.000
They are going to obstruct and get in the
way and blah, blah, blah, blah, blah.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.930
Joe Biden's proposal is for one point nine
trillion dollars.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.730
These Republicans want 618 billion.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:45.980
And they met yesterday with Joe Biden.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:52.100
So I think that the meeting with them is fine
as long as Joe Biden and Democrats are ready

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.170
to say, listen.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:57.990
Remember, they promised 2000 dollar checks
would go out right away.

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:02.930
It's February now, right away we could debate
what right away means and government speak.

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:07.430
But Joe Biden definitely made us think, John
USCIRF definitely made us think that the checks

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:08.800
were going out quickly.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:10.390
It's been a couple of weeks almost now.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:16.249
OK, so it's time to do it, have the meeting
with the Republicans, but understand that

00:02:16.249 --> 00:02:19.239
Republicans are going to make all sorts of
demands.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:23.359
They are going to demand capitulation to their
ideology, to their platform.

00:02:23.359 --> 00:02:24.970
They will weaken the bill.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:27.579
They will weaken the impact of the bill.

00:02:27.579 --> 00:02:32.430
And ultimately, even if you come up with something
that's between 600 billion and one point nine

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:37.409
trillion, they'll probably still refuse to
vote for it anyway.

00:02:37.409 --> 00:02:40.670
OK, these are not good faith actors.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:44.310
So don't be mad that Joe Biden is meeting
with Republicans.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.980
I'm fine with it.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.280
It's fine that he's doing it.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.689
He claimed he wants bipartisanship and unity
and all this stuff.

00:02:50.689 --> 00:02:51.760
That's fine.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.310
They were able to propose their six hundred
billion dollar package and they are likely

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.629
to vote against whatever compromise Democrats
end up proposing.

00:02:59.629 --> 00:03:04.370
So my view is give them a meeting and then
pass one point nine trillion without a single

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.980
Republican, if that's what they want to do.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:09.269
Now, you need Jim, if you don't get a single
Republican, you need Joe Manchin to vote.

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:13.219
And we need to be sure that Joe Manchin is
going to vote for it.

00:03:13.219 --> 00:03:14.390
Republicans will shriek.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:17.239
They will demand that they be met halfway.

00:03:17.239 --> 00:03:18.810
They will say, what about unity?

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:21.980
What about bipartisanship, blah, blah, blah.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:29.269
But when it's Democrats asking Republicans
to meet them halfway, when Trump is in power,

00:03:29.269 --> 00:03:30.620
remember what Republicans said?

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.920
Well, elections have consequences.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:36.190
We're not going to just because you guys want
this different thing.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.950
Trump won and we control this and we control
that.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:45.780
So Democrats should have a spine and be ready
because for an issue to have a compromise,

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:50.230
